<title>INDIA: Indian soybean steady; main markets shut.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean steady; main markets shut.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Soybean prices were steady in plant delivery conditions on Friday, dealers said, with all major markets in central India closed to mark a Hindu religious day. Business volumes were dull and the undertone easy.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices decreased by 100 rupees per tonne on increased selling against limited demand. Business volumes were dull and the undertone was easy.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices fell further on poor export demand. Soymeal yellow was $276-277 per tonne in export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $110 rupees per tonne for ready shipment and was $105 per tonne for March-April shipment in export. Rapeseed extraction was 3,750 rupees FOR Bedibunder for ready delivery and was 3,650 rupees per tonne for March-April delivery. The undertone was easy.</p>
